    "body": "In the Electrek Podcast , we discuss the most popular news in the world of sustainable transport and energy. In this week’s episode, we’ll discuss Tesla killing the Cybertruck, EVs surging in several key markets, and more.\nThe show is live every Friday at 4 p.m. ET on Electrek ’s YouTube channel .\nAs a reminder, we’ll have an accompanying post, like this one, on the site with an embedded link to the live stream. Head to the YouTube channel to get your questions and comments in.\nAfter the show ends at around 5 p.m. ET, the video will be archived on YouTube and the audio on all your favorite podcast apps:\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nApple Podcasts\nSpotify\nOvercast\nPocket Casts\nCastro\nRSS\nWe now have a Patreon if you want to help us avoid more ads and invest more in our content. We have some awesome gifts for our Patreons and more coming.\nHere are a few of the articles that we will discuss during the podcast:\nTesla to end Cybertruck production as sales stall at ~10% of plan\nTesla hikes Cybertruck prices up to 10% after announcing it will kill production\nLucid teases its cheaper sub-$50,000 Cosmos EV in new video and images\nBYD’s electric hypercar hits 312 mph, first production car over 500 km/h BYD’s 3,000-hp EV crashes at about 280 mph — Watch the driver escape unharmed\nBYD’s newest EV is about as big as a Toyota Camry, but brings a lot more tech for $23K\nElectric cars are about to overtake petrol in the UK, data shows\nGermany’s EV share hits record 37% as BEVs beat gas and diesel combined\nElectric trucks hit 50% of China’s heavy truck sales, diesel demand falls\nHere’s the live stream for today’s episode starting at 4:00 p.m. ET (or the video after 5 p.m. ET):\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on X , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
